    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n10666" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀντίφον-ος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>in revenge for blood,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ποινὰς ἀντιφόνους ἄτας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Eu.</u>
					982
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δώσουσ᾽ ἀντιφόνους δίκας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>El.</u>
					248
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀντίφονον κορέσαι στόμα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Ph.</u>
					1156
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θάνατοι ἀ.</span> deaths <i>by mutual
				slaughter,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Th.</u>
				893
			</span></i>.—Trag. word, but only in lyric passages.</div>
